<title>SOUTH AFRICA: Malbak says Lenco talks suspended.</title>
<headline>Malbak says Lenco talks suspended.</headline>
<dateline>JOHANNESBURG 1997-07-07</dateline>
<text>
<p>South African packaging firm Malbak Ltd said on Monday that its talks with Lenco Holdings Ltd, which may have had an effect on the firms' share prices, had been terminated.</p>
<p>No reasons were given for the termination of discussions other than to say that earlier cautionaries from both had thus been withdrawn.</p>
<p>In a separate announcement Malbak subsidiary Kohler Ltd said that unspecified talks in which it was engaged had also been ended. No further details were given.</p>
<p>The announcements follow a flood of rumours in the market that industrial conglomerate Rembrandt Group Ltd (Remgro) was set to buy Malbak through its Lenco Holdings Ltd unit.</p>
<p>Malbak, Kohler and Lenco had all issued cautionary announcements, saying they were in unspecified talks.</p>
<p>-- Johannesburg newsroom 27 11 482 1003</p>
